    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Persea barbujana</b></i>, the <b>Canary laurel</b> or <b>barbusano</b>, is a species of tree in the laurel family, Lauraceae. It is endemic to the Macaronesian islands of Madeira (incl. Porto Santo) and the Canary Islands. It is often placed as the sole species in genus <i>Apollonias</i>. Molecular phylogenic analyses found that the species is nested within the genus <i>Persea,</i> which also includes the Macaronesian endemic <i>Persea indica</i>.",
